{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/96348-what-was-the-arcana-of-the-dethroned-queen","id":96348,"title":"What was the arcana of the Dethroned Queen ?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-22T08:31:36-07:00","id":96348,"title":"What was the arcana of the Dethroned Queen ?","content":"Thanks.<br /> <br /> Suleri Drals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","name":"Suleri Drals","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-22T16:35:08-07:00","id":96581,"title":"","content":"No idea... it's likely that she didn't even necessarily walk a Path as we know them, since the Watchtowers didn't exist until after the Fall. So the answer is... whatever you want her arcana to be.<br /> <br /> According to RotE, she &quot;forsook all magic&quot; after being Dethroned anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-23T06:32:15-07:00","id":96853,"title":"","content":"Exarchs walks no a Path but they are no ever associated with a arcana ? (except Gate Exarch of the Abyss)<br /> Father is Exarch of Prime,ect....<br /> <br /> My question must be recalled &quot;The Dethroned Queen was the Exarch of..?&quot; ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":343,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","user":"Suleri Drals","date":". 03-23-2014, 09:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","name":"Suleri Drals","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-23T08:09:11-07:00","id":96888,"title":"","content":"Well, since the 10 Arcana already have an Iron Seal each, she likely was not one of them <i>or </i>if she was she has been fully replaced <i>or</i> she was an Iron Seal and there is actually an empty slot now, unbeknownst to the Seers at large, which could actually be a nice plot hook, if you want to run with that. But really, we do not know much about her real magical capabilities, so you can run with whatever you like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-23T08:42:39-07:00","id":96898,"title":"","content":"This is not a canon answer.<br /> <br /> Well, the Detroned Queen has been Dethroned. <br /> <br /> So you can imagine that any one of the other Arcana have an associated Exarch, you can think that:<br /> <br /> - It was another arcana, unknown to us. Since she has been dethroned (and her throne is in the material realm, not in the Heavens), it is not possible to use such Arcana.<br /> <br /> - Some of the other Exarchs De-throned her. Choose one arcana (i would say Prime) and rule that she fought with that exarch for being associated to that particular Arcana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1304-baroqo","name":"Baroqo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T12:41:14-07:00","id":98572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baroqo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/96348-what-was-the-arcana-of-the-dethroned-queen?p=96898#post96898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is not a canon answer.<br /> <br /> Well, the Detroned Queen has been Dethroned.<br /> <br /> So you can imagine that any one of the other Arcana have an associated Exarch, you can think that:<br /> <br /> - It was another arcana, unknown to us. Since she has been dethroned (and her throne is in the material realm, not in the Heavens), it is not possible to use such Arcana.<br /> <br /> <b>- Some of the other Exarchs De-throned her. Choose one arcana (i would say Prime) and rule that she fought with that exarch for being associated to that particular Arcana.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I prefer that, I do not see how a arcana could be added without being a doubled bloom of a another arcana. (10 is already much and recovers all that exists<br /> <br /> Moreover, that would break a certain symbolism numerologic. (I always believed that the ten arcanas correspond to the ten sefirots + Abyss/Ocean Ouroboros like Daat; the \u201csefirot\u201d which binds the various divine emanations in the same Unity.<br /> in the garden of Eden, become the No-sefirot when Adam with eaten the prohibited fruit and creates distorts the division between the man and the woman, the mundane world and the divine world, the false division of the aspects of the existence.*)<br /> <br /> *Daat is the sefirot knowledge of itself and the limits between all things; Daat channels the divine lights being divided since Kether (Binnah and Hokmah, the two sides of the tree, the pillar of the mercy and the pillar of severity, Daath being in the medium, centers pillar of balance) to return it in only one pure light towards Malkuth (The Physical World) so that this can being the pure reflection of the divine will (The Light of Kether; Will of God which is the thing nearest to Him that the Man can understand: Ein Sof is god himself, completely inaccessible and similar to the the Empyrean)<br /> The original sin having transformed Daat into the quasi-insuperable pit between the divine and the man; will and reality.<br /> Thus breaking the harmony between the arcanas because Daat is the center and the link of all the tree of life.<br /> <br /> What i say can be complety false since the versions of the kabbalah; of course; this is just a audacious interpretation for a tabletop game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","name":"Suleri Drals","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T12:41:04-07:00","id":101427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baroqo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/96348-what-was-the-arcana-of-the-dethroned-queen?p=96898#post96898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> - Some of the other Exarchs De-throned her. Choose one arcana (i would say Prime) and rule that she fought with that exarch for being associated to that particular Arcana.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why Prime ? (Passage of the Mother Goddess and paganism to patriarchal monotheistic religion ?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","name":"Suleri Drals","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T14:24:01-07:00","id":101493,"title":"","content":"I dont quiet get all this, battling with the ruling iron seal for control of the arcana. The way I've followed things the Exarch is the symbolic ruler of that Arcana, not the literal source. If that Exarch suddenly died that Arcana would be fine. And there are more Exarchs than there are 10 Arcana. Those are just the main Exarchs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1510-mysticjackal","name":"MysticJackal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1510_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T03:54:59-08:00","id":1031525,"title":"","content":"Her artifacts and its arcana are:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Ring Of The Dethroned Queen (Prime?)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Robe Of The Dethroned Queen (Space 3, Forces 4)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Scepter Of The Dethroned Queen (Prime 4)<br /> Crown Of The Dethroned Queen (Mind 4, 5)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Throne Of The Exarchs (Space ?)</span></span><br /> <br /> Whatever Arcana she was an exarch of is not mentioned anywhere in <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Reign of The Exarchs.</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11799-rbawintrow","name":"RBAWintrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11799_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T04:12:13-08:00","id":1031529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RBAWintrow</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/96348-what-was-the-arcana-of-the-dethroned-queen?p=1031525#post1031525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whatever Arcana she was an exarch of is not mentioned anywhere in <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Reign of The Exarchs.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Probably because she wasn't an Exarch of an arcana, there are probably more than just 10 Exarchs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T00:35:16-08:00","id":1036478,"title":"","content":"I thought there were more than ten Exarchs? Something about the Exarchs being &quot;innumerable&quot;. Don't remember where I read that, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T00:48:51-08:00","id":1036480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/96348-what-was-the-arcana-of-the-dethroned-queen?p=1036478#post1036478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought there were more than ten Exarchs? Something about the Exarchs being &quot;innumerable&quot;. Don't remember where I read that, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a common belief in the Seers, but it's presented as pretty clearly wishful thinking. (Doesn't mean it's wrong, just the Seers don't actually know.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T00:49:52-08:00","id":1036481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/96348-what-was-the-arcana-of-the-dethroned-queen?p=1036478#post1036478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought there were more than ten Exarchs? Something about the Exarchs being &quot;innumerable&quot;. Don't remember where I read that, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Seers' splatbook.<br /> <br /> &quot;Below the Iron Seals, the Seers of the Throne populate choruses and legions of lesser Exarchs. They speak of 8 million recording gods, seven legions of Arch-Ascended under every Seal, ruling 77 ochemata and 777 secret masters of the world, and even universes within each Exarch\u2019s soul, huge enough to spawn infinite avatars. The Seers are generous in naming Exarchs, because to do otherwise would suggest that the path to Ascension isn\u2019t attainable.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T00:53:34-08:00","id":1036483,"title":"","content":"I love 'arch-ascended'. Second only to 'Super-mega-ultra Ascended'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T01:56:37-08:00","id":1036498,"title":"","content":"Damn, that's a lot of Exarchs, theoretical or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T04:01:52-08:00","id":1036528,"title":"","content":"Yep, from a potential ignorant position I could see the Exarchs reaching possibly into a hundred members or so from the start, and since then there may have been a dozen or two dozen Exarchs that have been kicked out or destroyed by their fellow Exarchs. While if the Seers have it right and new Exarchs are created maybe half a dozen Seers have ascended to become new Exarchs and no Seers have ever ascended if we're going with what I think is the case in this matter.<br /> <br /> \u200bThese potentially new Exarchs would naturally be significantly less powerful than the OG Exarchs. Kind of like Sauron to Morgoth if you want an non-CoD explination.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T06:29:10-08:00","id":1036575,"title":"","content":"I'd assume the relative potency of a lesser Exarch, going with the assumption where there are more than 10+1, would scale with the effectiveness and insidiousness of the form of control and tyranny they are. This is why the ten Exarchs are so powerful - their form of tyranny are intrinsically tied to the Arcana themselves, and among them the four Archigenitors are the most successful in the modern world.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, do we know what form of control the non-Archigenitors are? The Archigenitors are control through religion, violence, nationalism, and surveillance. What exactly are the other six again? I only know they're related intimately to the Arcana.<br /> <br /> And if the Dethroned Queen indeed was an Exarch, what form of control would she have been? Now that she's been ousted, there's at least one thing that cannot be used to tyrannize humanity, unless another Exarch Ascended to take that niche. Assuming that didn't happen, what could the Dethroned Queen have been?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T07:01:35-08:00","id":1036591,"title":"","content":"Th Seers book details the other of the big 10 Exarchs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T07:10:59-08:00","id":1036597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/96348-what-was-the-arcana-of-the-dethroned-queen?p=1036591#post1036591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Th Seers book details the other of the big 10 Exarchs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which I sadly lack.<br /> <br /> I always assumed it was fatalism for the Ruin (&quot;none of what you do would matter anyway in the long run&quot;), elitism for the Prophet (&quot;only the chosen ones of history can guide the foolish masses&quot;), necrophobia for the Psychopomp (&quot;death is pain, so dance to my tune to avoid it&quot;), materialism for the Chancellor (&quot;everything can be reduced to its material worth&quot;), apathy for the Nemesis (&quot;you are not responsible for the pain you do not knowingly inflict&quot;), and animalism for the Raptor (&quot;humans are nothing but animals driven by base desires&quot;).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T07:31:23-08:00","id":1036607,"title":"","content":"I don't remember about the last two, but the rest are spot on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T07:45:32-08:00","id":1036617,"title":"","content":"The last one is more or less right as well. The Nemesis not so much. It's detailed as simply being the divide between spirit and material, It's not really elaborated much and there'd almost certainly be a bit more too it, in the same way that there's more going on with the Spirit Arcana than simply powers for affecting the beings in Forsaken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T07:59:59-08:00","id":1036626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/96348-what-was-the-arcana-of-the-dethroned-queen?p=1036607#post1036607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't remember about the last two, but the rest are spot on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yay for me, then!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/96348-what-was-the-arcana-of-the-dethroned-queen?p=1036617#post1036617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The last one is more or less right as well. The Nemesis not so much. It's detailed as simply being the divide between spirit and material, It's not really elaborated much and there'd almost certainly be a bit more too it, in the same way that there's more going on with the Spirit Arcana than simply powers for affecting the beings in Forsaken.</div> </div> </div> </div>I figured that if the Spirit Arcanum is about repercussions of your actions in the form of Resonance, which warps the environment to reinforce itself through positive feedback, then the Exarch who controls humanity through it would be about making people oblivious to the true extent of the impacts of their actions, both in themselves and their surroundings. This is how mages (well, techincally how I) explain why the Gauntlet is thick in places where many humans gather - it's a law of heaven that blinds the masses from seeing just exactly what their petty actions have wrought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T13:40:10-08:00","id":1036807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/96348-what-was-the-arcana-of-the-dethroned-queen?p=1036626#post1036626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I figured that if the Spirit Arcanum is about repercussions of your actions in the form of Resonance, which warps the environment to reinforce itself through positive feedback, then the Exarch who controls humanity through it would be about making people oblivious to the true extent of the impacts of their actions, both in themselves and their surroundings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now you say it, that's actually spot on. It just states it in rather mechanistic terms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is how mages (well, techincally how I) explain why the Gauntlet is thick in places where many humans gather - it's a law of heaven that blinds the masses from seeing just exactly what their petty actions have wrought. </div> </div> </div>There is a slight issue with that. The Gauntlet is a historical phenomena, it didn't always exist. I guess, the Nemesis might be tied to the more basic fact that spirits and the things they represent are dislocated. Way back in Tome of the Watchtowers it's noticable that the Primal Wild was described as a place where things were indivisible from their spirits.<br /> <br /> Also, there is an explanation floating around the books for the thickening of the Gauntlet. Essentially, humans produce a huge amount of essence and that churns up the gauntlet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T02:10:06-08:00","id":1037093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/96348-what-was-the-arcana-of-the-dethroned-queen?p=1036807#post1036807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is a slight issue with that. The Gauntlet is a historical phenomena, it didn't always exist. I guess, the Nemesis might be tied to the more basic fact that spirits and the things they represent are dislocated. Way back in Tome of the Watchtowers it's noticable that the Primal Wild was described as a place where things were indivisible from their spirits.<br /> <br /> Also, there is an explanation floating around the books for the thickening of the Gauntlet. Essentially, humans produce a huge amount of essence and that churns up the gauntlet.</div> </div> </div> </div>My idea is that the Supernal existence of the Nemesis seals Urfarah's fate and the rise of the Gauntlet. As Above, So Below. Even if some werewolves traveled back in time to stop Urfarah's death, some confluence of coincidences will ensure that Urfarah will die and Pangaea be lost, as long as the throne of the Nemesis exists in the Supernal.<br /> <br /> This makes the name of the Exarch of Spirit more interesting. He is called the Nemesis, because She comes out of the blue to levy punishments on mortals for sins and hubris they often don't even realize they committed, made worse by the fact that He's the one who blinded the mortals to their actions in the first place. Yet at the same time, She is called the Nemesis because that's exactly what He is... to the Uratha. She is the metaphysical reason why the race has been Forsaken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T06:41:32-08:00","id":1037161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/96348-what-was-the-arcana-of-the-dethroned-queen?p=1037093#post1037093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My idea is that the Supernal existence of the Nemesis seals Urfarah's fate and the rise of the Gauntlet. As Above, So Below. Even if some werewolves traveled back in time to stop Urfarah's death, some confluence of coincidences will ensure that Urfarah will die and Pangaea be lost, as long as the throne of the Nemesis exists in the Supernal.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's certainly possible but it feels a bit like 'God works in mysterious ways'. I mean, the other Exarchs affect the world in an eternal sense, they always were and always will be, Why not just build the gauntlet into the world?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This makes the name of the Exarch of Spirit more interesting. He is called the Nemesis, because She comes out of the blue to levy punishments on mortals for sins and hubris they often don't even realize they committed, made worse by the fact that He's the one who blinded the mortals to their actions in the first place. </div> </div> </div>You know, I always wondered why it was called Nemesis. Maybe that's obvious to everyone but me, but that's brilliant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T06:59:57-08:00","id":1037175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/96348-what-was-the-arcana-of-the-dethroned-queen?p=1037161#post1037161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's certainly possible but it feels a bit like 'God works in mysterious ways'. I mean, the other Exarchs affect the world in an eternal sense, they always were and always will be, Why not just build the gauntlet into the world?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's horrible, but the Exarchs (and the Oracles) really are Gods in the Mage cosmology, so Mysterious Ways isn't that out-of-character for them.<br /> <br /> But yeah, my idea makes the Nemesis the odd one out by making His dominion over the world have a defined moment in history.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T23:28:15-08:00","id":1037691,"title":"","content":"If I remember Imperial Mysteries correctly then there are several lesser exarchs. It's the final reward for those most faithful. Most end up merging with their preferred iron seal though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","name":"cmwatford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T00:05:24-08:00","id":1037695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/96348-what-was-the-arcana-of-the-dethroned-queen?p=1037093#post1037093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He is called the Nemesis, because She comes out of the blue to levy punishments on mortals for sins and hubris they often don't even realize they committed, made worse by the fact that He's the one who blinded the mortals to their actions in the first place. Yet at the same time, She is called the Nemesis because that's exactly what He is... to the Uratha. She is the metaphysical reason why the race has been Forsaken.</div> </div> </div> </div>What if Nemesis ASCENDED by the killing of Urfarah? Like there could be other Iron Seal of Spirit before, but it's Nemesis plot and manipulation of both Uratha and Luna that make him Exarch he is now, dethroning his predecessor?<br /> <br /> Dethroned Queen from Reign of Exarchs - based on her Artifacts - sounds to me more like previous Iron Seal of Prime or Space. Myself, I would make her dethroned as matriarchy was removed from society. As patriarchy is Prime, matriarchy would also be Prime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-25-2017, 03:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T00:10:34-08:00","id":1037696,"title":"","content":"I've always seen the Nemesis as the &quot;fear of the unknown&quot;- it is the enemy in the dark, always watching, whispering on the back of your neck only that when you turn around- no one is there. It is the paranoia that leads to madness, a fear which is not rational or understand- but a primal doubt of existence which makes you keep a small light in the night, to keep the demons away- and bring madness upon those who cross the worlds so all shall remain in their protected homes, deep in a safe cave in which all you can see are shadows. <br /> <br /> In sort, he is the Exarch of madness, superstition and fear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T03:19:24-08:00","id":1037735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/96348-what-was-the-arcana-of-the-dethroned-queen?p=1037695#post1037695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What if Nemesis ASCENDED by the killing of Urfarah? Like there could be other Iron Seal of Spirit before, but it's Nemesis plot and manipulation of both Uratha and Luna that make him Exarch he is now, dethroning his predecessor?</div> </div> </div> </div>That certainly makes sense. While I haven't read Imperial Mysteries (but should, like Axelgear said in another thread), that's how those Omen things work right? A major global event required to Ascend?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Dethroned Queen from Reign of Exarchs - based on her Artifacts - sounds to me more like previous Iron Seal of Prime or Space. Myself, I would make her dethroned as matriarchy was removed from society. As patriarchy is Prime, matriarchy would also be Prime. </div> </div> </div>Maybe, coupled with the above idea, the Dethroned Queen was actually the Exarch of Spirit, prior to the Nemesis? Her Artifacts don't use Spirit, because she's been barred from accessing her greatest power by the new Iron Seal, so she gets on by with her lesser Arcana.<br /> <br /> It also kinda makes sense for her to be the lost Exarch of matriarchy, regardless of Arcana associated. Recent researches in anthropology shows that a matriarchal society, as opposed to patriarchal societies, never existed in the sense that we modern people think (or more correctly, what older feminists envisioned). Maybe in the Mage verse, true matriarchy existed when the Queen was still a God, but got erased from reality when she was Dethroned. This also has disquieting implications - matriarchy as a former tool of tyranny? It's hard to think, but...<br /> <br /> (Oh, and there's that Obrimos-Thyrsus contrast that lines up with the monotheism-paganism divide, which also lines up with patriarchy-matriarchy divide)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/96348-what-was-the-arcana-of-the-dethroned-queen?p=1037696#post1037696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always seen the Nemesis as the &quot;fear of the unknown&quot;- it is the enemy in the dark, always watching, whispering on the back of your neck only that when you turn around- no one is there. It is the paranoia that leads to madness, a fear which is not rational or understand- but a primal doubt of existence which makes you keep a small light in the night, to keep the demons away- and bring madness upon those who cross the worlds so all shall remain in their protected homes, deep in a safe cave in which all you can see are shadows.<br /> <br /> In sort, he is the Exarch of madness, superstition and fear.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, if the Nemesis is the fear of the unknown, then would the Raptor be the fear of the known? As in, the fear of natural predators and the dangers of the wilderness? That also makes sense.<br /> <br /> It's also possible for it to be both, right? The Nemesis is spiritual obliviousness and the fear of the unknown, and the Raptor is animalism and the fear of the wild. Together, they reduce humans from brave pioneers of the corners of the world into weak-willed cowards who rely on the chosen shamans of the Gods to bring wisdom, warping the ideals of the Thyrsus Path.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 01-25-2017, 06:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T12:58:20-08:00","id":1037996,"title":"","content":"You could identify the Queen with the Moros Oracle. The mechanics of her ascension are quite similiar to how the Moros Oracle supposedly created the Watchtower. You die to ascend.<br /> <br /> Also, The Father is patriarchial, not the Exarch of Patriarchy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/96348-what-was-the-arcana-of-the-dethroned-queen?p=1037175#post1037175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's horrible, but the Exarchs (and the Oracles) really are Gods in the Mage cosmology, so Mysterious Ways isn't that out-of-character for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. 'mysterious ways' thing is a reason given for why God does/doesn't do things you might expect them to. It's basically admitting you don't know, but you still have faith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}